{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ce4mV9M7SQQxaugUa4KNN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Placement Decision\n\n**Where to add it:**\n\nFold the new rule into the existing bullet \"**Retries are bounded and jittered.**\" in §2, as a trailing sentence after the current text.\n\n**Edited region:**\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Failure handling\n\n- **Retries are bounded and jittered.** Every retry wrapper declares\n  its maximum attempt count at the call site; backoff is exponential\n  with jitter, and a non-retriable error class aborts immediately —\n  enumerate those classes beside the wrapper, not in a distant\n  constants file. A retry wrapper must also cap total elapsed time,\n  not only attempt count, so declare both the attempt cap and the\n  wall-clock cap at the call site; a per-attempt timeout with\n  unbounded attempts still hangs the caller.\n- **Timeouts are explicit.** No call inherits a library default\n  timeout silently; the call site states its per-attempt timeout.\n```\n\n**Rationale:**\n\nThe new statement constrains *retry bounding* — it adds a second dimension (wall-clock cap) to the attempt-count cap already governed by the first bullet. The existing bullet already owns the topic of what a retry wrapper must declare at the call site; the new rule is a direct elaboration of that constraint, not a separate concern. Folding it into the host bullet (rather than creating a standalone one) keeps related retry-declaration requirements together and avoids duplication with the neighboring timeout bullet."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":337,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
